			"notes": "## 12 languages, and how to read them\n\n**New languages to learn:** French, German, Italian, Portuguese (Brazil), Japanese, Korean, Chinese (Simplified) and Hindi, alongside Spanish, Russian, Romanian and Hebrew. Pick one in Settings (K) → Language to learn. Each language keeps its own progress.\n\n**Readings:** words in another alphabet show how to say them in small Latin letters, in the popup and in your dictionary (J):\n\n| | Word | Reading |\n|---|---|---|\n| Hebrew | לפיד | Lapid |\n| Japanese | 羽根 | Hane |\n| Korean | 뼈다귀 | Ppyeodagwi |\n| Chinese | 鸡蛋 | Jī dàn |\n| Hindi | धागा | Dhaaga |\n| Russian | Торт | Tort |\n\n**Fixes**\n- Hindi vowel signs and Japanese ゛ marks are no longer ignored when checking answers.\n- Chinese and Japanese answers count anywhere inside a longer phrase (these languages don't put spaces between words).\n\n**Known limits**\n- Minecraft's font draws Hindi vowel signs detached from their letters. The reading underneath shows how to say the word.\n- Voice answers in Japanese, Korean, Chinese and Hindi are untested.\n\n**Update:** remove `say-it-or-lose-it-0.2.0.jar` from your mods folder and add `say-it-or-lose-it-0.3.0.jar`. Your settings and progress carry over.\n\nsha256 `cab9ba81f1c87e59b3ae693f8a98ccb59f792ec619ad7a53c3b1220ea125649a`"
		},
